    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0202" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.51/78: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-20T15:00:00-05:00">October 20, 1914—3
                            p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Your number 67, October 16th, 6 P. M. This Government would view with much
                    satisfaction the negotiation of a commercial treaty with Russia along the lines
                    indicated in the first of the two conditions upon which Count Witte makes his
                    acceptance of a mission to the United States depend. Do I understand that it is
                    Count Witte’s desire to come as a special envoy to negotiate such a treaty or
                    that he desires the treaty to be signed before he visits this country?</p>
                <p>Please advise the Department promptly as to any further developments in regard to
                    the subject. It would be manifestly improper for this Government to take any
                    part in facilitating a loan to one of the belligerent governments. It would not
                    be frank to lead Count Witte, whose stipulations as you report them do him so
                    much honour, to expect this.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d137-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d137-f1" n="4" xml:id="d137-f1-content">
                <p>The last two sentences were added on the draft telegram in President Wilson’s
                    hand (file No. 861.51/78½).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
